-- title:
--   Sections miss generic points of special-fibre components
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero and $p$ prime, a proof $h_{pN_0}$ that $p \nmid N_0$, and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{P} :$ `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀` for level $N_0p$. Let $O$ be a local ring equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from the base ring `DRLevel.R p`, and assume $\mathfrak{m}_O = (p)$, the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $O$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a ring homomorphism $t_\kappa : O \to \kappa$, and let $R$ be a resolved model package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`: this provides an integral, locally Noetherian scheme $R.Y$, proper and flat over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ via $R.\mathtt{toBase}$, proper over the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model via $R.\mathtt{toDR}$, regular with stalks of Krull dimension at most $2$ at all points lying over the closed locus where $p$ is not invertible, an isomorphism onto the smooth locus and over the locus where $p$ is invertible, a finite set of nodes with widths $R.\mathtt{width} \ge 1$ matched with the crossing points of the two $\kappa$-fibre components, invertible integral ideal sheaves $R.\mathtt{comp}\, v$ indexed by $v \in$ `X0MqComponents R.width` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_{n}\mathrm{Fin}(R.\mathtt{width}(n)-1)$ with support in the fibre over $(p)$ and with $\prod_v R.\mathtt{comp}\,v$ cutting out $(p)$ on every affine open, together with points $R.\eta\,v \in R.Y$ attached to these components. Let $\sigma : \operatorname{Spec} O \to R.Y$ satisfy $\sigma$ followed by $R.\mathtt{toBase}$ equal to the identity, and let $c$ be any index in `X0MqComponents R.width`. Then the point $R.\eta\,c$ does not lie in the image of the map $\sigma.\mathtt{base}$ on underlying topological spaces.
--
--   This is the standard fact that an $O$-valued section of a regular arithmetic surface avoids the generic points of the components of its special fibre; here the surface is the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0p)$ over a local ring with maximal ideal $(p)$, and the components are the two strict transforms together with the chains of exceptional components at the nodes. It is used in the computation of intersection numbers and Euler characteristics on the special fibre, in particular by the lemma evaluating the Euler characteristic of sections of pullbacks of the ideal sheaf of $\sigma$ against products of component ideals.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackageLevel_eta_notMem_range_of_comp_toBase_eq_id.lean

